WEBVTT

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.931
Captain's Log,
Stardate 54274.7.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.735
Lieutenant Torres has
finally convinced me

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:09.900
that I can't put off

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.240
a major maintenance overhaul
any longer.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.177
We've set down on
an uninhabited planet,

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.715
and I've sent shuttles
to search for supplies.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.614
What about the
impulse upgrades?

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.674
Day after tomorrow.

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.618
Put a new phase compensator
on that relay.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.087
Environmental control?

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.317
The thermal regulators are
still running a little hot.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:26.916
Too bad we can't just
keep the windows open.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.585
How long until the warp drive
is back on line?

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.593
Six days.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.129
You sure you can't get
it done any faster?

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.859
Captain, I don't like sitting
still any more than you do,

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.527
but repairs
this extensive take time.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.569
Mendez, track down
that power drain.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.571
Right away.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.164
I know this ship
has been through

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.676
a lot, but you told me
this would only take a few days.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.803
That was before I discovered
the microfractures

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.869
in the starboard nacelle

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.778
and the fused relays
in the main computer.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.245
Who did that?

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:58.113
I noticed a charge imbalance
in the EPS feed.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.681
I'm sorry if I...

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.351
It could have taken us hours
to find that.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:04.920
I have a tactical
systems report for you.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.589
It's from
Commander Tuvok.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.725
I'd say you're capable
of a lot more

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.497
than delivering padds, Icheb.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.764
I agree.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.932
Until we get underway again,
he's assigned to you.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.305
With him on your team,

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:19.277
maybe you'll get this job done
a little faster.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.483
Neelix?

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.658
Rise and shine. It's 0500.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.257
Already?

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.529
Oh!

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.867
Oh, I was dreaming
we found the dilithium

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.964
and were back aboard Voyager.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.669
Dreaming is
an accurate description.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.075
Didn't we already
scan this nebula?

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.512
Four times.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.880
I thought the Borg
were known for being thorough.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:01.387
The Borg value efficiency,
not redundancy.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.081
I've got a hunch
about this nebula.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.919
There's dilithium
in there somewhere.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:09.852
I'm getting some fluctuating

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:10.725
energy readings.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.025
From the nebula?

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.998
No, it's weapons fire.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.009
Let's get out of here.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.517
We're receiving a distress call.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.416
...have casualties.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:15.954
Please help us.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.114
We're on a humanitarian mission

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:21.626
delivering medical supplies.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.163
Reverse course.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:29.633
We can't just leave them.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:30.930
Starfleet policy.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:33.870
Interference in alien conflicts
is strictly prohibited.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.067
You heard their Captain.
It's a medical ship.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.142
Their shields are down.

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:40.236
Life support is failing
on at least three decks.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.746
Open a channel
to the other ship.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:48.516
This is Ensign Kim
of the Delta Flyer.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.681
I don't know what
you're fighting about,

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.315
but it looks like you've won.

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:54.952
The people on the other ship
have casualties. We'd like to...

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.050
This isn't your concern.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.063
I'm not taking sides.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.758
I only want to
help the wounded.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:03.324
Withdraw immediately.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.268
They're charging weapons.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:07.898
Neelix, set our deflector beam

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.771
for a narrow pulse.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.070
Seven, let me know

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.442
the second their weapons array
is fully charged.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.344
I might be able
to trigger an overload.

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:17.713
The deflector bandwidth
is at.4 microns.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:19.251
Now.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.321
Their weapons are off-line.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.416
Shields are down.

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.928
They're retreating.

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:32.224
Take the helm.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.890
Neelix, you're with me.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.094
Who's in charge here?

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.632
He is.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.327
What are we going to do?

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:11.393
It's okay.
We're here to help.

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:13.837
The ship that attacked
you is gone.

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.396
Who are you?

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:17.340
Harry Kim from
the Starship Voyager.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.503
We're responding
to your distress call.

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:21.171
We can treat

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.578
your wounded.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.919
The Captain?

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.044
Dead, sir.

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:31.215
So are the rest
of the officers.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:35.283
I'm reading a total of 27
life-forms aboard the ship.

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:36.453
There were 56 of us.

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.087
How are we going to get home

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:39.358
without the officers?

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.161
We need to restore main power.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.826
Where's the warp interface?

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:45.132
We're passengers, not crewmen.

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:48.105
You can access
engineering systems from here.

00:06:56.783 --> 00:07:00.344
Your warp core's intact.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.581
I think I can bring it
back on line.

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:04.623
Can you monitor
antimatter flow?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.681
I'm not sure. I...

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.386
Just watch this readout,

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:09.621
and tell me

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.720
if it starts to fluctuate.

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:23.204
I'm routing emergency power
to structural

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:24.573
integrity.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:27.078
Atmospheric pressure
is returning to normal.

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.914
Neelix, we'll go through
the ship deck by deck...

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:33.474
find the survivors.

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:35.817
We need to get our cloak
back on line.

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:38.322
I'll take a look at it as soon
as I've repaired the engines.

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:40.382
No. The cloak is more important.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.361
The Annari have far more
powerful weapons than we do.

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:44.361
If they come back,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.091
the cloak is our best defense.

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.133
We'll try to get it
back on line.

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:55.634
Kim to Delta Flyer.

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:57.039
Go ahead.

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:58.133
I need your help, Seven.

00:07:58.211 --> 00:08:00.338
It looks like we're going
to be here for awhile.

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:04.714
How did you do it?

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:05.978
Do what?

00:08:06.052 --> 00:08:08.612
Disable the Annari warship
so quickly?

00:08:08.688 --> 00:08:10.019
Uh, basically, we used

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:11.886
their own weapons against them.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:13.548
How?

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:15.856
We used a deflector pulse

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.828
to overload their phaser banks.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.735
You know a lot
about engineering.

00:08:23.803 --> 00:08:26.772
It's all part
of my Starfleet training.

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:28.101
Starfleet?

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:29.801
Yeah. The organization
I work for.

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:31.810
And they teach you
all these things?

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:33.106
We train at an academy,

00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:35.773
and I guess I've picked up
a few new tricks

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:37.475
during my time on Voyager.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.313
How long have you been Captain?

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:41.884
I'm just an Ensign.

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:44.582
Ensign? E... What's that?

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:46.420
A junior officer.

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:49.984
The lowest ranked officer,
actually.

00:08:52.331 --> 00:08:55.494
This is my first
deep space assignment.

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:57.661
It hasn't gone very well.

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:01.436
Could you hand me that?

00:09:03.676 --> 00:09:06.474
My first week on the job
didn't go very well, either.

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:08.878
We ended up 70,000

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:10.312
light-years from home,

00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:12.874
lost over a dozen crew members,

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:16.581
but I got through it,
and so will you.

00:09:18.357 --> 00:09:20.655
I hope so.

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:23.559
If you're going to be
a starship officer,

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:27.588
you've got to accept that
adversity comes with the job.

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:42.914
What's that?

00:09:43.049 --> 00:09:44.038
It's a diagnostic

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:45.777
of the antimatter injectors.

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:48.115
No, I meant that
stuff you're eating.

00:09:48.187 --> 00:09:49.882
Nutritional supplements,

00:09:49.956 --> 00:09:52.652
replicated to meet
my metabolic requirements.

00:09:52.725 --> 00:09:53.919
Sounds delicious.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:57.518
You know, in the Mess Hall,

00:09:57.597 --> 00:10:01.556
they actually have
tables and chairs for that.

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:03.226
I prefer to work while I eat.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:05.429
It's a more efficient
use of my time.

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:10.433
You did a great job today.

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:13.808
We're ahead of schedule
thanks to you.

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:17.838
Here's what we're going
to work on tomorrow.

00:10:19.418 --> 00:10:22.649
I'll see you at 0600.

00:10:28.194 --> 00:10:30.128
Icheb.

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:31.493
Yes?

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:33.225
What do you do for fun?

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:34.926
Fun?

00:10:35.001 --> 00:10:36.263
Recreation.

00:10:36.335 --> 00:10:38.428
How do you spend your time
when you're off duty?

00:10:38.504 --> 00:10:40.404
Between my work and my studies,

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:42.839
I don't have much time
for recreation.

00:10:42.908 --> 00:10:46.537
I've learned that you've got
to take a break once in awhile.

00:10:46.612 --> 00:10:48.910
I've been doing a lot
of rock climbing

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:50.812
on the holodeck.

00:10:50.883 --> 00:10:52.180
Maybe when we're finished

00:10:52.251 --> 00:10:53.980
tightening all
the nuts and bolts,

00:10:54.053 --> 00:10:55.213
you'd like to join me.

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:58.586
I do have an interest
in geology.

00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:00.990
It's not about the rocks, Icheb.

00:11:01.093 --> 00:11:02.958
It's about the climbing.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:13.031
Main power has been restored.

00:11:13.105 --> 00:11:14.936
All stations responding.

00:11:15.041 --> 00:11:17.373
The cloak's back on line.

00:11:17.443 --> 00:11:20.241
Impulse and warp drives
are standing by.

00:11:20.312 --> 00:11:22.872
Shields are at 96 percent.

00:11:22.948 --> 00:11:24.939
I'd say you're ready
to get back on course.

00:11:25.017 --> 00:11:26.109
We appreciate your help.

00:11:26.185 --> 00:11:27.618
I hope you have
a safe journey.

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:28.881
Mr. Kim...

00:11:28.954 --> 00:11:31.946
I feel guilty
asking even more of you,

00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:35.721
but no one on this ship
knows how to fly it.

00:11:35.795 --> 00:11:40.494
None of you has ever piloted
a starship?

00:11:40.566 --> 00:11:42.557
I've trained in shuttles,

00:11:42.635 --> 00:11:44.500
but nothing like this.

00:11:46.739 --> 00:11:49.799
I'll enter a flight plan
in the auto-navigation system

00:11:49.875 --> 00:11:52.571
and give you a quick course
in helm operations.

00:11:52.645 --> 00:11:54.442
You shouldn't have any trouble.

00:11:54.513 --> 00:11:55.502
Couldn't you take us?

00:11:55.581 --> 00:11:56.878
This ship needs

00:11:56.949 --> 00:11:59.144
an experienced
commanding officer.

00:11:59.218 --> 00:12:01.618
I'm sorry, but we've already
gotten more involved

00:12:01.687 --> 00:12:02.619
than we should have,

00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:04.246
and they need us
back on Voyager.

00:12:04.323 --> 00:12:06.188
It's not just my ship
that concerns me.

00:12:06.258 --> 00:12:08.488
You've made an enemy
of the Annari now,

00:12:08.561 --> 00:12:11.086
but if you dock your ship
in our Shuttle Bay,

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:12.630
our cloak will protect you.

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:15.531
That's a generous offer,
but we'll be fine.

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:18.263
Please, Mr. Kim,
we can't afford to fail.

00:12:18.337 --> 00:12:19.827
This ship is...

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:21.770
Loken, don't.

00:12:21.841 --> 00:12:24.776
We can trust these people.

00:12:24.844 --> 00:12:27.210
I'm a doctor.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:29.839
These people are
my research team.

00:12:29.915 --> 00:12:32.543
We're carrying new vaccines
to our homeland.

00:12:32.618 --> 00:12:34.518
They'll save thousands
of lives.

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:37.488
Sir, I looked at
their flight plan.

00:12:37.556 --> 00:12:41.117
It takes them pretty
close to Voyager.

00:12:43.329 --> 00:12:45.820
I'll bring you
as far as our ship.

00:12:45.898 --> 00:12:47.126
When we get there,

00:12:47.199 --> 00:12:50.657
you can discuss your situation
with my Captain.

00:12:50.736 --> 00:12:52.431
Thank you.

00:12:52.505 --> 00:12:54.496
What about Starfleet policy?

00:12:54.573 --> 00:12:56.837
This is a
humanitarian mission.

00:12:56.909 --> 00:13:00.072
Dock the Flyer
in their Shuttle Bay.

00:13:07.987 --> 00:13:10.615
We're approaching the planet.

00:13:10.689 --> 00:13:12.452
Take us out of warp.

00:13:12.525 --> 00:13:14.049
Disengage the cloak.

00:13:14.126 --> 00:13:15.457
Wait.

00:13:15.528 --> 00:13:18.793
I'm detecting three
alien vessels in orbit.

00:13:18.864 --> 00:13:20.058
On screen.

00:13:22.835 --> 00:13:24.427
Those are Annari warships.

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:26.198
Your people are in danger.

00:13:39.118 --> 00:13:41.211
I apologize
for the state of my ship.

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:42.720
We weren't
expecting company.

00:13:42.788 --> 00:13:44.085
I hope we're not imposing.

00:13:44.156 --> 00:13:45.088
Not at all.

00:13:45.157 --> 00:13:46.488
Making contact
with new cultures

00:13:46.559 --> 00:13:47.753
is a priority for us.

00:13:47.827 --> 00:13:49.454
For us, too.

00:13:49.528 --> 00:13:50.961
This is a fine ship, Captain.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:52.725
One of the best in the fleet,

00:13:52.798 --> 00:13:54.356
but it could use a new set

00:13:54.433 --> 00:13:56.060
of deuterium injectors.

00:13:56.135 --> 00:13:58.660
Any chance you
could provide them?

00:13:58.737 --> 00:14:01.171
I think
we can arrange something.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.867
What are you offering
in exchange?

00:14:02.942 --> 00:14:04.068
Zeolitic ore.

00:14:04.143 --> 00:14:06.737
We mined several tons of it
from an asteroid field.

00:14:06.812 --> 00:14:08.404
It's high-grade,
easy to refine.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.107
I'll speak
to my supply officer.

00:14:11.317 --> 00:14:12.375
We're being hailed

00:14:12.451 --> 00:14:14.248
by Ensign Kim, audio only.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:15.787
Hello, Harry.

00:14:15.855 --> 00:14:17.345
Is everything all right?

00:14:17.423 --> 00:14:18.822
Of course.
Why wouldn't it be?

00:14:18.891 --> 00:14:22.258
Our long-range scans
detected several alien ships

00:14:22.328 --> 00:14:23.420
orbiting the planet.

00:14:23.495 --> 00:14:24.928
I appreciate your concern,

00:14:24.997 --> 00:14:26.362
but there's nothing
to worry about.

00:14:26.432 --> 00:14:28.024
We've made some new friends,
that's all.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.192
When can we expect you back?

00:14:29.268 --> 00:14:31.395
We've run into a slight delay.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.097
Nothing serious, I hope.

00:14:33.172 --> 00:14:35.163
No. Everything's under control.

00:14:35.241 --> 00:14:36.401
Good.

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:38.136
Any luck finding dilithium?

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:39.643
Uh, I'm afraid not.

00:14:39.712 --> 00:14:41.612
I'll tell the other teams
to keep looking.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:42.612
See you soon, Ensign.

00:14:42.681 --> 00:14:44.205
Yes, ma'am. Kim out.

00:14:44.283 --> 00:14:45.682
Dilithium...

00:14:45.751 --> 00:14:47.412
We can get that for you, too.

00:14:47.486 --> 00:14:48.919
Really?

00:14:49.955 --> 00:14:52.947
She's formed an alliance
with our enemy.

00:14:53.058 --> 00:14:54.525
Just because they're talking

00:14:54.593 --> 00:14:56.220
doesn't mean
they formed an alliance.

00:14:56.295 --> 00:14:58.354
It's probably just
a friendly meeting.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.057
That's how the Annari operate.

00:15:00.132 --> 00:15:01.360
They come to you as friends,

00:15:01.433 --> 00:15:02.866
and when they've won your trust,

00:15:02.935 --> 00:15:06.462
they declare you subjects
of the Annari Empire.

00:15:10.542 --> 00:15:12.510
Kim to Voyager.

00:15:12.578 --> 00:15:14.341
We didn't expect you so soon.

00:15:14.413 --> 00:15:16.438
Actually, Captain,
I'm closer than I let on.

00:15:16.515 --> 00:15:18.642
And I've brought
some new friends of my own.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.745
Our chances of getting home
without your help

00:15:23.822 --> 00:15:25.653
aren't very good.

00:15:25.724 --> 00:15:28.454
We'd appreciate any assistance
you could offer.

00:15:28.527 --> 00:15:30.461
I hope you understand.

00:15:30.529 --> 00:15:32.656
I need to give this
some thought.

00:15:43.976 --> 00:15:47.412
You've put me in
a difficult position, Ensign.

00:15:47.479 --> 00:15:49.709
We could use the help
the Annari are offering,

00:15:49.782 --> 00:15:51.943
but if they find out
we're aiding their enemy...

00:15:52.051 --> 00:15:53.746
I couldn't just stand
by and do nothing.

00:15:53.819 --> 00:15:55.252
That doesn't justify

00:15:55.321 --> 00:15:57.289
getting involved
in somebody else's fight.

00:15:57.356 --> 00:15:59.620
What would you have done?

00:15:59.692 --> 00:16:01.626
Probably exactly what you did.

00:16:01.694 --> 00:16:03.662
I guess I learned from the best.

00:16:03.729 --> 00:16:06.391
If this were simply an errand
of mercy, I wouldn't hesitate.

00:16:06.465 --> 00:16:08.399
But the fact is,
these people are involved

00:16:08.467 --> 00:16:10.401
in an interplanetary war.

00:16:10.469 --> 00:16:12.266
Captain,
I've gotten to know them

00:16:12.338 --> 00:16:13.896
over the last couple of days.

00:16:14.039 --> 00:16:15.666
You met Loken.

00:16:15.741 --> 00:16:17.834
They're scientists,
not soldiers.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.878
You've only heard
one side of the story.

00:16:19.945 --> 00:16:21.537
You've taken sides before.

00:16:21.613 --> 00:16:22.705
The Borg resistance,

00:16:22.781 --> 00:16:23.577
the Vaadwaur...

00:16:23.649 --> 00:16:25.480
Those were
different circumstances.

00:16:25.551 --> 00:16:27.178
You were trying
to help people in need.

00:16:27.252 --> 00:16:29.311
How is this any different?

00:16:29.388 --> 00:16:30.753
Have you thought about applying

00:16:30.823 --> 00:16:32.256
to the Advocate General's
office?

00:16:32.324 --> 00:16:33.916
You'd make a good lawyer.

00:16:36.495 --> 00:16:37.723
I suppose I could spare

00:16:37.796 --> 00:16:39.423
Chakotay or Tuvok
for a few days.

00:16:39.498 --> 00:16:41.125
That won't be necessary.

00:16:42.968 --> 00:16:44.663
The Kraylor know me.

00:16:44.737 --> 00:16:45.931
They trust me.

00:16:46.005 --> 00:16:47.939
I'm sure they'd find Tuvok
or Chakotay

00:16:48.007 --> 00:16:49.497
just as trustworthy.

00:16:49.575 --> 00:16:52.237
But they outrank me.

00:16:52.311 --> 00:16:55.280
If you send one of them,
it won't be my mission anymore.

00:16:55.347 --> 00:16:57.338
Your mission.

00:16:57.416 --> 00:16:59.441
My first real command.

00:16:59.518 --> 00:17:01.452
You've been in command
on Voyager before.

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.681
On the night shift,
for a few hours...

00:17:03.756 --> 00:17:05.383
It's not the same thing.

00:17:05.457 --> 00:17:08.153
You and Chakotay are
always a couple of decks away,

00:17:08.227 --> 00:17:10.559
ready to take over if
anything goes wrong.

00:17:10.629 --> 00:17:12.859
I've been on Voyager
for almost seven years,

00:17:12.931 --> 00:17:14.455
and I'm still an Ensign.

00:17:14.533 --> 00:17:17.400
If this is your way
of bucking for a promotion...

00:17:17.469 --> 00:17:20.734
No, no, I understand
there's a command structure

00:17:20.806 --> 00:17:23.274
and that our circumstances
are unique.

00:17:23.342 --> 00:17:25.833
But the fact is,
if we were back home,

00:17:25.911 --> 00:17:27.606
I'd be a Lieutenant by now,

00:17:27.679 --> 00:17:29.909
maybe even
a Lieutenant Commander.

00:17:30.049 --> 00:17:33.143
You're pretty sure
of yourself, aren't you?

00:17:33.218 --> 00:17:35.015
I know I can do this,

00:17:35.087 --> 00:17:37.783
and the Kraylor are giving me
a chance to prove it.

00:17:39.825 --> 00:17:43.056
I expect you back before
we complete our repairs.

00:17:43.128 --> 00:17:44.459
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:45.462
And I'm not

00:17:45.531 --> 00:17:46.463
sending you alone.

00:17:46.532 --> 00:17:47.464
Captain.

00:17:47.533 --> 00:17:49.364
I want you
to take Seven.

00:17:49.435 --> 00:17:53.064
Since she has no rank,
you clearly outrank her.

00:18:00.913 --> 00:18:03.040
Lieutenant Torres asked me

00:18:03.115 --> 00:18:05.345
to repair a malfunctioning
holo-emitter.

00:18:05.417 --> 00:18:07.248
It's about time.

00:18:07.319 --> 00:18:09.446
Whenever I move
to the far corner

00:18:09.521 --> 00:18:12.115
of the Surgical Bay,
my legs disappear.

00:18:16.261 --> 00:18:20.357
Seven of Nine told me
you gave her social lessons.

00:18:20.432 --> 00:18:23.458
Hm. She wanted to get along
better with the crew.

00:18:23.535 --> 00:18:27.301
Social skills are one thing
the Borg never assimilated.

00:18:27.372 --> 00:18:29.340
I was hoping
you could instruct me, as well.

00:18:29.408 --> 00:18:30.340
I'd be delighted.

00:18:30.409 --> 00:18:31.899
Lesson One: "Making
a First lmpression."

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.170
Actually...

00:18:33.245 --> 00:18:35.304
I wanted to ask you
about something specific.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.007
Fire away.

00:18:37.082 --> 00:18:39.573
How can you tell
when someone has...

00:18:39.651 --> 00:18:42.552
romantic feelings for you?

00:18:42.621 --> 00:18:44.748
Icheb, this is a surprise.

00:18:44.823 --> 00:18:47.223
Have you caught someone's eye?

00:18:47.292 --> 00:18:50.557
I'm speaking hypothetically.

00:18:50.629 --> 00:18:52.290
Ah.

00:18:53.532 --> 00:18:55.329
Hypothetically,

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:57.368
there are various indications

00:18:57.436 --> 00:18:59.028
of romantic attraction.

00:18:59.104 --> 00:19:00.765
Compliments, for example,

00:19:00.839 --> 00:19:03.740
invitations to
social activities,

00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:07.245
finding excuses to be in close
proximity with someone.

00:19:07.312 --> 00:19:09.280
Yes, but couldn't
those things happen

00:19:09.348 --> 00:19:11.475
in a relationship
that wasn't romantic?

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:12.778
I suppose.

00:19:12.851 --> 00:19:15.149
Is there a way
to be absolutely certain?

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:18.314
Well, short of an open
declaration of affection,

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:20.290
there are some
fairly reliable

00:19:20.359 --> 00:19:21.883
physiological responses:

00:19:21.994 --> 00:19:24.189
Elevated blood pressure,
increased

00:19:24.263 --> 00:19:26.060
beta-endorphin production...

00:19:26.131 --> 00:19:29.066
Thank you, Doctor.
You've been very helpful.

00:19:29.134 --> 00:19:31.659
With my guidance, you
will master the nuances

00:19:31.737 --> 00:19:33.728
of social interaction
in no time!

00:19:36.041 --> 00:19:37.906
Harry!

00:19:38.043 --> 00:19:39.408
Take me with you, buddy.

00:19:39.478 --> 00:19:41.173
Sorry, Tom. This is my mission.

00:19:41.246 --> 00:19:43.908
Oh, come on, I've been itching
to get back into space

00:19:44.049 --> 00:19:46.176
ever since we set down
on this dust bowl.

00:19:46.251 --> 00:19:47.809
I'm tired of cleaning conduits

00:19:47.886 --> 00:19:49.012
and replacing relays.

00:19:49.087 --> 00:19:50.111
You're a married man now.

00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:51.679
You've got family
responsibilities.

00:19:51.757 --> 00:19:52.883
Just leave the away missions

00:19:52.958 --> 00:19:54.220
to the young,
unattached guys.

00:19:54.293 --> 00:19:55.658
That ship is in
pretty bad shape.

00:19:55.727 --> 00:19:57.160
You're going to
need a good pilot.

00:19:57.229 --> 00:19:58.594
No, thanks.

00:19:58.664 --> 00:20:00.598
Wait a minute...

00:20:00.666 --> 00:20:02.861
I know what
this is about.

00:20:02.935 --> 00:20:03.867
You do?

00:20:03.936 --> 00:20:05.801
Sure. You've got a girl
on that ship

00:20:05.871 --> 00:20:07.600
you don't want me
to know about.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.603
There's no girl. Not this time.

00:20:10.676 --> 00:20:13.008
Then what is it?

00:20:14.213 --> 00:20:15.737
I don't know how else
to this say this,

00:20:15.814 --> 00:20:16.746
so I'll just say it.

00:20:16.815 --> 00:20:18.282
You've always been
Captain Proton.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:21.183
I have always
been Buster Kincaid.

00:20:21.253 --> 00:20:22.777
It's my turn this time.

00:20:36.301 --> 00:20:38.531
I'm glad you're not
planning to leave

00:20:38.604 --> 00:20:40.333
on an empty
stomach, "Captain."

00:20:40.405 --> 00:20:41.963
I have...

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:43.940
plomeek soup
and eggplant parmesan.

00:20:44.009 --> 00:20:45.237
Either's fine.

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:46.242
Wrong answer.

00:20:46.311 --> 00:20:47.300
Excuse me?

00:20:47.379 --> 00:20:49.074
If you're going
to be a Captain,

00:20:49.147 --> 00:20:50.876
you have to act like a Captain.

00:20:50.949 --> 00:20:53.440
Never admit you're
uncertain about anything.

00:20:53.518 --> 00:20:56.078
You can't be indecisive
in front of your crew.

00:20:56.154 --> 00:20:58.486
It's just a snack, Neelix.

00:20:58.557 --> 00:21:00.752
When Captain Janeway
comes in here,

00:21:00.826 --> 00:21:02.919
she knows exactly
what she wants.

00:21:03.061 --> 00:21:05.291
Maybe I'm just not as picky
about my food.

00:21:05.364 --> 00:21:09.528
Whatever you say... Ensign.

00:21:09.601 --> 00:21:10.829
Neelix.

00:21:12.337 --> 00:21:15.636
Plomeek soup,
and make sure it's hot.

00:21:23.749 --> 00:21:25.717
Captain on the Bridge.

00:21:27.252 --> 00:21:28.651
Where did you learn that?

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.652
I've been studying

00:21:29.721 --> 00:21:31.450
that Starfleet manual
you loaned me.

00:21:31.523 --> 00:21:33.047
Take your station, Mr. Terek.

00:21:33.125 --> 00:21:35.252
Aye, sir.

00:21:35.327 --> 00:21:36.453
Course?

00:21:36.528 --> 00:21:38.257
I'll do it.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:42.391
Laying in a course,
heading 115 mark 37.

00:21:43.802 --> 00:21:45.736
Does this ship
have a name?

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:48.671
Medical Transport 136.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:51.072
I think we can do
better than that.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:57.448
Nightingale.

00:21:57.516 --> 00:21:59.484
The name of someone
from my homeworld.

00:21:59.551 --> 00:22:00.916
She was famous for treating

00:22:00.986 --> 00:22:03.819
wounded soldiers
on the battlefield.

00:22:03.889 --> 00:22:05.516
It's perfect.

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:07.854
Hail Voyager.

00:22:09.494 --> 00:22:10.722
Kim to Voyager.

00:22:10.796 --> 00:22:12.263
We're ready to get underway.

00:22:12.331 --> 00:22:14.822
Acknowledged. Good luck.

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:16.094
See you in a few days.

00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:17.100
Kim out.

00:22:17.169 --> 00:22:18.329
Main power.

00:22:18.403 --> 00:22:20.166
- On line.
- Tactical.

00:22:20.238 --> 00:22:23.105
Shields and weapons standing by.

00:22:23.175 --> 00:22:26.235
Bring the cloak on line.

00:22:26.311 --> 00:22:28.279
Warp 6.

00:22:30.082 --> 00:22:32.050
Engage.

00:22:41.426 --> 00:22:46.193
Acting Captain's Personal Log,
Stardate 54277.3.

00:22:46.264 --> 00:22:48.357
My first day in command
has been challenging,

00:22:48.433 --> 00:22:50.526
but I've loved
every minute of it.

00:22:50.602 --> 00:22:53.628
I can't help feeling that this
was something I was born to do.

00:22:53.705 --> 00:22:57.766
The hourly status report
you requested.

00:22:57.843 --> 00:22:58.901
Thanks.

00:22:58.977 --> 00:23:02.413
Why have you brought
these items aboard?

00:23:02.481 --> 00:23:04.642
They make me
feel more at home.

00:23:04.716 --> 00:23:07.310
We'll only be on this
vessel for a few days.

00:23:07.386 --> 00:23:09.877
Decorating is an inefficient
use of your time.

00:23:09.955 --> 00:23:12.651
It's important to forge
a personal connection

00:23:12.724 --> 00:23:15.192
with your vessel;
make the ship your own.

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:16.488
Ask Captain Janeway.

00:23:16.561 --> 00:23:20.190
I'll discuss it with her
the moment we return.

00:23:21.666 --> 00:23:23.190
Is there anything else?

00:23:23.268 --> 00:23:25.202
I asked Terek
to make a course correction.

00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:26.931
He's never done that before.

00:23:27.038 --> 00:23:28.471
I'd better check on him.

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:31.304
I believe he's capable
of doing it himself.

00:23:39.017 --> 00:23:40.279
Status?

00:23:40.352 --> 00:23:41.944
I've entered the new heading.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.578
Looks like the guidance vector

00:23:43.655 --> 00:23:45.282
is off by a couple of microns.

00:23:45.357 --> 00:23:47.291
I was about to correct that.

00:23:47.359 --> 00:23:48.519
You need to realign

00:23:48.593 --> 00:23:50.959
the primary
navigational sensor first.

00:23:51.029 --> 00:23:52.326
Yes, sir.

00:23:53.298 --> 00:23:54.959
And make sure
it stays locked

00:23:55.066 --> 00:23:56.192
on your guide star.

00:23:56.268 --> 00:23:57.599
Here, let me show you.

00:24:10.982 --> 00:24:12.381
I'm-I'm sorry, Lieutenant.

00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:13.748
Don't worry about it.

00:24:13.819 --> 00:24:15.912
Bumping elbows
comes with the job,

00:24:15.987 --> 00:24:18.182
and you can
call me B'Elanna.

00:24:18.256 --> 00:24:20.281
Put this with the others.

00:24:23.662 --> 00:24:26.529
These relays should have been
replaced a while ago.

00:24:26.598 --> 00:24:28.759
It's amazing
they've held up this long.

00:24:28.834 --> 00:24:30.597
I am really
looking forward

00:24:30.669 --> 00:24:32.933
to our climb.

00:24:33.004 --> 00:24:33.936
Wouldn't you prefer

00:24:34.039 --> 00:24:36.303
to spend your free time
with your husband?

00:24:38.009 --> 00:24:40.671
If it doesn't involve
a race car, a shuttle,

00:24:40.745 --> 00:24:44.044
or something else he can drive,
Tom's not interested.

00:24:44.115 --> 00:24:45.776
Besides, since we got married,

00:24:45.851 --> 00:24:47.614
I see more
than enough of him.

00:24:47.686 --> 00:24:48.983
Hold still.

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:02.592
What's that?

00:25:02.667 --> 00:25:03.759
I'm reading a power fluctuation

00:25:03.835 --> 00:25:05.063
somewhere
in the propulsion system.

00:25:05.136 --> 00:25:06.398
It's destabilizing the cloak.

00:25:06.471 --> 00:25:07.438
All stop.

00:25:17.315 --> 00:25:18.748
Core is stable.

00:25:18.817 --> 00:25:20.910
That should take
care of it.

00:25:20.986 --> 00:25:22.681
Are you absolutely certain?

00:25:22.754 --> 00:25:24.722
As a scientist,
you should know

00:25:24.789 --> 00:25:27.656
there's no such thing
as absolute certainty.

00:25:27.726 --> 00:25:29.591
Perhaps we could run
a diagnostic before we...

00:25:29.661 --> 00:25:30.753
That would take hours.

00:25:30.829 --> 00:25:32.524
Captain Janeway
wants us back

00:25:32.597 --> 00:25:34.258
before Voyager
finishes its overhaul.

00:25:34.332 --> 00:25:35.731
The cloaking system
is delicate.

00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:37.199
It requires
constant attention.

00:25:37.269 --> 00:25:38.258
Correct me if I'm wrong,

00:25:38.336 --> 00:25:39.496
you're a physician.

00:25:40.906 --> 00:25:42.737
You have to trust me on this.

00:25:42.807 --> 00:25:45.275
We'll monitor it closely.
Don't worry.

00:25:45.343 --> 00:25:47.140
I simply want to ensure

00:25:47.212 --> 00:25:49.646
that our mission is a success.

00:25:49.714 --> 00:25:52.376
You asked me
to take command of this ship,

00:25:52.450 --> 00:25:54.179
and that's what I'm doing.

00:26:01.626 --> 00:26:03.093
Tell Terek to resume course.

00:26:08.266 --> 00:26:10.257
I've discovered a serious flaw

00:26:10.335 --> 00:26:12.235
in one of the ship's systems.

00:26:12.304 --> 00:26:13.293
Which one?

00:26:13.371 --> 00:26:14.531
The Captain.

00:26:16.575 --> 00:26:17.837
The Captain's main function

00:26:17.909 --> 00:26:19.376
is to issue orders, correct?

00:26:19.444 --> 00:26:21.207
- Right.
- And the crew's function

00:26:21.279 --> 00:26:23.873
is to support the Captain
and carry out those orders.

00:26:23.949 --> 00:26:25.610
What's your point?

00:26:25.684 --> 00:26:28.084
Every time you give an order,
you carry it out yourself.

00:26:28.153 --> 00:26:29.916
And when someone else
makes a suggestion,

00:26:29.988 --> 00:26:31.046
you dismiss it.

00:26:31.122 --> 00:26:33.147
These people are inexperienced.

00:26:33.224 --> 00:26:34.452
They need my help.

00:26:34.526 --> 00:26:36.494
When you first came
aboard Voyager,

00:26:36.561 --> 00:26:38.324
did Captain Janeway help you?

00:26:38.396 --> 00:26:41.456
Sure. She looked after
all the junior officers.

00:26:41.533 --> 00:26:43.023
By doing your work for you?

00:26:43.101 --> 00:26:44.534
No. She gave me a lot to do,
actually.

00:26:44.603 --> 00:26:45.627
Because she felt

00:26:45.704 --> 00:26:47.934
you were more capable
than she was?

00:26:48.073 --> 00:26:49.665
Of course not.

00:26:49.741 --> 00:26:54.735
She wanted me to learn,
to gain confidence.

00:26:54.813 --> 00:26:56.110
Interesting.

00:27:06.758 --> 00:27:07.884
Emergency power.

00:27:07.959 --> 00:27:09.756
Repolarize
the containment field.

00:27:09.828 --> 00:27:10.886
I can't.

00:27:10.962 --> 00:27:12.224
The cloak is going
to fail again.

00:27:12.297 --> 00:27:13.889
Don't panic.
This is a minor malfunction.

00:27:13.965 --> 00:27:15.734
Minor? We're losing
our main defense system.

00:27:16.735 --> 00:27:19.226
We've been detected.

00:27:19.304 --> 00:27:22.102
Two Annari vessels are
closing on our position.

00:27:22.173 --> 00:27:24.801
Correction...
six Annari vessels.

00:27:32.651 --> 00:27:33.811
Evasive maneuvers!

00:27:34.986 --> 00:27:36.510
Kim to Engineering.

00:27:36.588 --> 00:27:39.056
Go ahead.

00:27:39.124 --> 00:27:40.751
We need that cloak
back on line.

00:27:40.825 --> 00:27:43.055
The primary generator
has failed.

00:27:43.128 --> 00:27:44.220
I'm trying to...

00:27:46.331 --> 00:27:48.265
Seven?

00:27:48.333 --> 00:27:50.028
Seven, come in.

00:27:50.101 --> 00:27:52.399
You have the Bridge.

00:27:52.470 --> 00:27:53.596
We need you here.

00:27:53.672 --> 00:27:54.764
I'll go, sir.

00:27:56.608 --> 00:27:59.270
All right. I'll give you
instructions over the com.

00:28:00.712 --> 00:28:01.872
Charge phaser banks.

00:28:01.946 --> 00:28:03.538
Target their weapons array.

00:28:03.615 --> 00:28:04.707
Which ship?

00:28:04.783 --> 00:28:08.241
The closest one,
off our port bow.

00:28:19.130 --> 00:28:20.563
Dayla to the Bridge.

00:28:20.632 --> 00:28:22.429
Life support's failing
down here.

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:24.900
I've gotten everyone out.

00:28:24.969 --> 00:28:26.095
Good work.

00:28:26.171 --> 00:28:28.162
Now go
to the cloaking generator.

00:28:28.239 --> 00:28:29.900
What's the field polarity?

00:28:29.974 --> 00:28:31.066
206.4.

00:28:31.142 --> 00:28:32.234
That's too low.

00:28:32.310 --> 00:28:33.902
We're going to have to raise it.

00:28:33.978 --> 00:28:35.639
I'm bypassing
the phase converter.

00:28:35.714 --> 00:28:37.909
Wait. I didn't tell you
to do that.

00:28:38.049 --> 00:28:40.108
Won't that increase
the field polarity?

00:28:40.185 --> 00:28:41.277
Yes, but...

00:28:42.487 --> 00:28:44.216
Listen to me carefully.

00:28:44.289 --> 00:28:45.813
I want you to try...

00:28:45.890 --> 00:28:47.255
Dayla, it's Loken.

00:28:47.325 --> 00:28:48.349
Take the warp core off-line.

00:28:48.426 --> 00:28:50.087
What are you talking about?

00:28:50.161 --> 00:28:52.652
Bypass the driver coil
and shunt power directly

00:28:52.731 --> 00:28:54.460
to the polaron matrix.

00:29:04.042 --> 00:29:05.703
The cloak is back on line.

00:29:05.777 --> 00:29:07.142
Get us out of here,
full impulse.

00:29:07.212 --> 00:29:08.873
Dayla, secure

00:29:08.947 --> 00:29:10.073
the Engineering section

00:29:10.148 --> 00:29:11.479
and get back to the Bridge.

00:29:13.284 --> 00:29:15.377
Dayla!

00:29:17.722 --> 00:29:20.156
I'm not reading
any life signs in Engineering.

00:29:32.203 --> 00:29:33.227
Dayla?

00:29:33.304 --> 00:29:34.828
She's dead.

00:29:34.906 --> 00:29:36.806
How's Seven?

00:29:36.875 --> 00:29:38.740
She may be in shock.

00:29:38.810 --> 00:29:40.903
I'm not sure.

00:29:41.012 --> 00:29:42.604
Have a look.

00:29:51.956 --> 00:29:54.618
Your opinion, Doctor?

00:29:54.692 --> 00:29:58.150
I believe
she may be in shock.

00:29:58.229 --> 00:29:59.355
Do you think
we should give her

00:29:59.430 --> 00:30:00.362
a cortical stimulant?

00:30:00.431 --> 00:30:02.661
That might be indicated.

00:30:05.003 --> 00:30:06.595
You are no doctor, are you?

00:30:09.207 --> 00:30:10.674
You and I need to talk...

00:30:10.742 --> 00:30:12.107
alone.

00:30:20.852 --> 00:30:22.786
What the hell is going on?

00:30:22.854 --> 00:30:24.549
I don't know what you mean.

00:30:24.622 --> 00:30:27.113
Nothing about this
mission is adding up.

00:30:27.192 --> 00:30:29.183
It's obvious you
know a lot more

00:30:29.260 --> 00:30:31.524
about cloaking systems
than biology.

00:30:31.596 --> 00:30:32.688
So did Dayla.

00:30:32.764 --> 00:30:33.696
And the second

00:30:33.765 --> 00:30:34.857
our cloak failed,

00:30:34.933 --> 00:30:38.164
half a dozen Annari warships
came after us...

00:30:38.236 --> 00:30:41.694
one little medical transport.

00:30:41.773 --> 00:30:43.400
The truth!

00:30:46.177 --> 00:30:49.874
My colleagues and I have
been working at a secret base

00:30:49.948 --> 00:30:51.813
but not to create vaccines.

00:30:51.883 --> 00:30:55.319
We've been developing
cloaking devices for our fleet.

00:30:55.386 --> 00:30:56.910
This ship is a prototype.

00:30:56.988 --> 00:30:58.922
The Annari know we have it,

00:30:58.990 --> 00:31:00.685
and they don't want
us to get it home.

00:31:00.758 --> 00:31:02.419
I never would
have agreed to this

00:31:02.493 --> 00:31:04.825
if I had known you had
a military objective.

00:31:04.896 --> 00:31:08.730
Our world has been under an
Annari blockade for three years.

00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:11.496
The planet is protected
by a shield grid,

00:31:11.569 --> 00:31:15.266
but it's almost impossible
to get our ships in or out.

00:31:15.340 --> 00:31:18.275
I convinced Captain Janeway
this was a humanitarian mission.

00:31:18.343 --> 00:31:19.571
It is.

00:31:19.644 --> 00:31:24.047
The Annari are choking us
to death slowly.

00:31:24.115 --> 00:31:27.243
If we can't get supply ships
through the blockade,

00:31:27.318 --> 00:31:30.082
we can't get food
to our people...

00:31:30.154 --> 00:31:31.644
or medicine.

00:31:31.723 --> 00:31:36.683
For all I know,
that's another lie.

00:31:43.034 --> 00:31:44.126
Reverse course.

00:31:44.202 --> 00:31:45.134
Sir?

00:31:45.203 --> 00:31:46.761
We're heading back to Voyager.

00:31:46.838 --> 00:31:47.930
I don't understand.

00:31:48.006 --> 00:31:50.201
He knows about the cloak.

00:31:50.275 --> 00:31:51.970
I would've told you...

00:31:52.076 --> 00:31:52.974
I gave you an order.

00:31:53.111 --> 00:31:53.975
What about the mission?

00:31:54.112 --> 00:31:54.976
That's not your concern.

00:31:55.113 --> 00:31:56.080
You want to be
a starship officer?

00:31:56.147 --> 00:31:57.136
Your job

00:31:57.215 --> 00:31:58.682
- is to follow orders.
- Sir, I don't think you...

00:31:58.750 --> 00:32:00.308
This is not a debate.

00:32:00.385 --> 00:32:02.512
You're under my command.

00:32:08.459 --> 00:32:10.051
No, sir.

00:32:10.128 --> 00:32:11.720
Not anymore.

00:32:11.796 --> 00:32:13.161
You're relieved.

00:32:13.231 --> 00:32:15.222
You, take the helm.

00:32:15.300 --> 00:32:18.531
I believe you're the one
who's been relieved.

00:32:26.377 --> 00:32:28.641
Where are you going
in such a hurry?

00:32:28.713 --> 00:32:31.477
Engineering,
to assist B'Elanna...

00:32:31.549 --> 00:32:33.039
Lieutenant Torres.

00:32:33.117 --> 00:32:35.551
Well, you've been seeing
a lot of my wife lately.

00:32:35.620 --> 00:32:36.951
Should I be worried?

00:32:37.088 --> 00:32:38.680
Mm, the repairs
are extensive.

00:32:38.756 --> 00:32:39.848
It's a lot of work.

00:32:39.924 --> 00:32:41.084
You can't fool me.

00:32:41.159 --> 00:32:44.219
I heard you two were planning
on scaling some cliffs together.

00:32:44.295 --> 00:32:45.557
It was her idea.

00:32:45.630 --> 00:32:46.722
Hey, relax.

00:32:46.798 --> 00:32:49.062
Spending time on the holodeck
is good for you,

00:32:49.133 --> 00:32:51.761
but if you really want
to have fun, forget climbing.

00:32:51.836 --> 00:32:53.497
Try my race car program.

00:32:53.571 --> 00:32:54.663
"Race car"?

00:32:54.739 --> 00:32:56.570
You get to chase me
around a track

00:32:56.641 --> 00:32:58.268
in an old Earth
ground vehicle.

00:32:58.343 --> 00:32:59.776
300 kph.

00:32:59.844 --> 00:33:01.869
It'll really get
your blood pumping.

00:33:01.946 --> 00:33:04.278
Are you challenging
me to a competition?

00:33:04.349 --> 00:33:06.442
Well, you think
you can take me?

00:33:06.517 --> 00:33:09.350
Tomorrow, Holodeck 2,
1900 hours.

00:33:24.402 --> 00:33:26.927
There is something
we need to discuss.

00:33:27.071 --> 00:33:29.733
Sure, as soon as you help me
finish this diagnostic.

00:33:29.807 --> 00:33:30.739
I can't do this.

00:33:30.808 --> 00:33:31.740
Of course you can.

00:33:31.809 --> 00:33:33.071
You've done
dozens of them.

00:33:33.144 --> 00:33:35.078
I'm not talking
about the diagnostic.

00:33:35.146 --> 00:33:36.579
I'm talking about us.

00:33:36.647 --> 00:33:37.739
"Us"?

00:33:37.815 --> 00:33:40.750
Your interest in me...
it's inappropriate.

00:33:40.818 --> 00:33:42.809
I don't think I understand.

00:33:42.887 --> 00:33:45.754
It's obvious you desire
a romantic involvement.

00:33:45.823 --> 00:33:47.085
Excuse me?

00:33:47.158 --> 00:33:49.149
You've made all the
customary overtures...

00:33:49.227 --> 00:33:51.627
finding reasons to
spend time with me,

00:33:51.696 --> 00:33:52.720
complimenting me,

00:33:52.797 --> 00:33:55.960
inviting me to engage in
recreational activities.

00:33:56.100 --> 00:33:58.091
Your husband
even challenged me

00:33:58.169 --> 00:33:59.397
to a ritual contest.

00:33:59.470 --> 00:34:01.165
What are you talking about?

00:34:01.239 --> 00:34:02.297
According to my research,

00:34:02.373 --> 00:34:03.897
it's a traditional
Klingon practice.

00:34:04.042 --> 00:34:07.910
Look... I'm sorry,
but you've got the wrong idea.

00:34:08.012 --> 00:34:10.105
You seemed a little lonely.

00:34:10.181 --> 00:34:12.274
I was just trying
to be friendly.

00:34:12.350 --> 00:34:13.408
I scanned you.

00:34:13.484 --> 00:34:14.473
You scanned me?

00:34:14.552 --> 00:34:15.814
In the Jefferies tube.

00:34:15.887 --> 00:34:18.481
Your blood pressure
and neurotransmitter readings

00:34:18.556 --> 00:34:20.080
indicated a state of arousal.

00:34:20.158 --> 00:34:23.525
It was hot, and I've been
under a lot of pressure,

00:34:23.594 --> 00:34:25.892
but I certainly wasn't aroused.

00:34:28.132 --> 00:34:30.225
Look, Icheb, I like you...

00:34:30.301 --> 00:34:35.500
but aside from the fact
that I am a much older woman,

00:34:35.573 --> 00:34:36.835
I'm married.

00:34:36.908 --> 00:34:39.468
That's why we have to do
the honorable thing.

00:34:40.778 --> 00:34:42.643
We should stop seeing
each other.

00:34:46.651 --> 00:34:49.381
You're right.

00:34:49.454 --> 00:34:51.319
As much as it hurts,

00:34:51.389 --> 00:34:54.324
I'll just have
to face the truth.

00:34:54.392 --> 00:34:56.223
It's for the best.

00:34:56.294 --> 00:34:57.591
Mm.

00:35:11.943 --> 00:35:13.911
Seven?

00:35:15.947 --> 00:35:17.881
Feeling better?

00:35:17.949 --> 00:35:19.883
Well enough to return to duty.

00:35:19.951 --> 00:35:22.385
You won't be returning to duty,

00:35:22.453 --> 00:35:24.717
not on this ship anyway.

00:35:24.789 --> 00:35:26.882
Loken lied to us.

00:35:26.958 --> 00:35:28.619
There's no vaccine.

00:35:28.693 --> 00:35:30.923
The cloak is the real cargo.

00:35:31.028 --> 00:35:33.929
I ordered the crew
to take us back to Voyager,

00:35:34.031 --> 00:35:35.498
but they refused.

00:35:35.566 --> 00:35:38.057
They mutinied.

00:35:38.136 --> 00:35:40.730
I guess that's what
you'd call it.

00:35:40.805 --> 00:35:42.898
I've packed some supplies.

00:35:42.974 --> 00:35:44.441
We'll take an escape pod.

00:35:44.509 --> 00:35:46.841
I'm hoping the Annari
will leave us alone,

00:35:46.911 --> 00:35:48.435
treat us as neutral parties.

00:35:48.513 --> 00:35:50.674
We're not "neutral parties."

00:35:50.748 --> 00:35:52.909
This is a military mission.
We can't get involved.

00:35:52.984 --> 00:35:54.246
We've been "involved"

00:35:54.318 --> 00:35:56.343
since you first fired
on that Annari ship.

00:35:56.420 --> 00:35:58.786
I thought I was helping people
in distress.

00:35:58.856 --> 00:36:01.051
Don't they still need your help?

00:36:01.125 --> 00:36:02.615
Are you abandoning this ship

00:36:02.693 --> 00:36:05.025
because the mission
wasn't what you expected

00:36:05.096 --> 00:36:07.894
or because being a Captain
wasn't what you expected?

00:36:07.965 --> 00:36:10.900
I am perfectly capable
of commanding a starship.

00:36:10.968 --> 00:36:12.299
Are you?

00:36:12.370 --> 00:36:14.338
Clearly, you're uncomfortable
with the role...

00:36:14.405 --> 00:36:15.895
delegating tasks, giving orders.

00:36:16.040 --> 00:36:17.905
Someone died
following my orders!

00:36:17.975 --> 00:36:20.273
You can't blame yourself
for that.

00:36:20.344 --> 00:36:22.209
A Captain's responsible
for the lives of his crew.

00:36:22.280 --> 00:36:24.646
People sometimes die
on missions,

00:36:24.715 --> 00:36:26.740
despite the Captain's
best efforts.

00:36:26.817 --> 00:36:30.082
I should have stuck to
playing Buster Kincaid.

00:36:30.154 --> 00:36:34.614
A holodeck program can be turned
off when it no longer suits you.

00:36:34.692 --> 00:36:36.557
Reality can't.

00:36:41.532 --> 00:36:44.592
If you really feel responsible
for this crew,

00:36:44.669 --> 00:36:46.432
you'll help them get home,

00:36:46.504 --> 00:36:49.268
because they won't survive
without you.

00:36:53.644 --> 00:36:57.171
Is that some new
kind of weapon?

00:36:57.248 --> 00:37:00.479
They're scanning pulses designed
to illuminate cloaked ships.

00:37:00.551 --> 00:37:02.712
If we hit one,
we'll be exposed.

00:37:02.787 --> 00:37:04.550
How are we going
to get through?

00:37:04.622 --> 00:37:06.817
We'll find a way.

00:37:06.891 --> 00:37:08.882
I thought you were leaving.

00:37:08.993 --> 00:37:11.461
I get claustrophobic
in escape pods.

00:37:11.529 --> 00:37:13.394
Switch to manual helm control.

00:37:13.464 --> 00:37:15.625
Full power to shields.

00:37:17.568 --> 00:37:19.832
Aye, Captain.

00:37:35.119 --> 00:37:37.087
Two Annari ships
have entered orbit.

00:37:37.154 --> 00:37:38.121
They are hailing.

00:37:38.189 --> 00:37:39.213
On screen.

00:37:39.290 --> 00:37:42.418
Captain Geral, we have
12 isotons of ore for you.

00:37:42.493 --> 00:37:45.462
I'm under orders to escort you
out of Annari space,

00:37:45.529 --> 00:37:47.019
immediately.

00:37:47.098 --> 00:37:48.622
You've been supporting
our enemy.

00:37:48.699 --> 00:37:49.927
You must be mistaken.

00:37:50.067 --> 00:37:50.931
A shuttlecraft

00:37:51.068 --> 00:37:52.592
matching your hull composition

00:37:52.670 --> 00:37:54.831
fired on one of our ships
several days ago.

00:37:54.905 --> 00:37:57.465
And we recently detected
two human bio-signatures

00:37:57.541 --> 00:37:58.940
on a Kraylor warship.

00:37:59.010 --> 00:38:00.272
I can explain that.

00:38:00.344 --> 00:38:01.572
If you don't leave immediately,

00:38:01.646 --> 00:38:03.477
we'll be forced to fire on you.

00:38:03.547 --> 00:38:06.072
Our warp drive
is still being repaired.

00:38:06.150 --> 00:38:08.710
Then we'll escort you
at impulse.

00:38:08.786 --> 00:38:11.118
You have five minutes
to lift off.

00:38:13.190 --> 00:38:15.158
So much for our new
deuterium injectors.

00:38:15.226 --> 00:38:16.818
What about Harry and Seven?

00:38:16.894 --> 00:38:18.191
We'll go looking for them,

00:38:18.262 --> 00:38:20.924
as soon as we get rid
of our escort.

00:38:28.072 --> 00:38:30.131
Evasive maneuvers.

00:38:31.309 --> 00:38:32.901
There are too many of them.

00:38:32.977 --> 00:38:34.239
You're doing fine.

00:38:34.312 --> 00:38:35.802
Just try to stay
at least 100 meters

00:38:35.880 --> 00:38:37.074
ahead of the closest pulse.

00:38:37.148 --> 00:38:38.706
Yes, sir.

00:38:39.784 --> 00:38:41.911
We should return fire.

00:38:41.986 --> 00:38:43.146
No, that would only give them

00:38:43.220 --> 00:38:44.949
another way to
triangulate our position.

00:38:48.926 --> 00:38:50.416
Our shields are failing.

00:38:50.494 --> 00:38:53.122
We're losing structural
integrity on the lower decks.

00:38:53.197 --> 00:38:54.892
Reroute emergency power.

00:38:55.966 --> 00:38:57.126
It's insufficient.

00:38:57.201 --> 00:38:59.795
Open a channel
to the lead Annari ship.

00:38:59.870 --> 00:39:01.030
Sir?

00:39:01.105 --> 00:39:01.867
Do it.

00:39:03.140 --> 00:39:05.233
Aye, sir.

00:39:06.844 --> 00:39:10.109
This is Captain Kim of
the Kraylor Vessel Nightingale.

00:39:10.181 --> 00:39:13.116
I'm prepared to discuss terms
for our surrender.

00:39:14.485 --> 00:39:15.543
End transmission.

00:39:15.619 --> 00:39:17.484
We trusted you.

00:39:17.555 --> 00:39:18.886
And you still should.

00:39:18.956 --> 00:39:20.048
They're responding.

00:39:20.124 --> 00:39:22.456
I don't have time to explain.

00:39:22.526 --> 00:39:23.550
On screen.

00:39:24.895 --> 00:39:27.420
Your surrender
will be unconditional.

00:39:27.498 --> 00:39:28.760
No, it won't.

00:39:28.833 --> 00:39:31.563
Either you allow my crew
to evacuate to the surface,

00:39:31.635 --> 00:39:33.466
or I'll put this ship
on self-destruct.

00:39:33.537 --> 00:39:34.834
You'll never get

00:39:34.905 --> 00:39:35.894
the cloaking technology.

00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:38.099
Something tells me
your superiors won't be happy

00:39:38.175 --> 00:39:40.336
about that.

00:39:40.411 --> 00:39:42.606
Your crew will be taken
aboard my vessel

00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:45.012
and brought
to an Annari detention center.

00:39:45.082 --> 00:39:47.073
My crew is going to the
surface in escape pods.

00:39:47.151 --> 00:39:49.278
Once they're clear,
you can lock on

00:39:49.353 --> 00:39:51.082
to this ship
with a tractor beam.

00:39:52.890 --> 00:39:53.879
Agreed.

00:39:53.958 --> 00:39:56.825
You've two minutes to evacuate.

00:39:56.894 --> 00:39:59.260
I will not abandon this ship.

00:39:59.330 --> 00:40:00.922
I'm glad to hear that,

00:40:00.998 --> 00:40:02.932
because I'm going
to need you here.

00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:05.332
Get your people into
the pods... quickly.

00:40:05.403 --> 00:40:06.665
But the cloak...

00:40:06.737 --> 00:40:08.102
I've got a plan to save it.

00:40:08.172 --> 00:40:10.663
If I fail, at least
the scientist who designed it

00:40:10.741 --> 00:40:12.606
will be alive
to create another one.

00:40:17.948 --> 00:40:21.406
Seven, scan the Annari's
tractor emitters.

00:40:21.485 --> 00:40:23.783
I need to know
the exact beam polarity.

00:40:23.854 --> 00:40:25.515
What are we going to do?

00:40:25.589 --> 00:40:28.456
Once they lock on to us,
they're going to come about

00:40:28.526 --> 00:40:29.959
and pull us away
from the planet.

00:40:30.094 --> 00:40:31.186
As soon as they do,

00:40:31.262 --> 00:40:33.253
we're going to reverse
our shield polarity.

00:40:33.330 --> 00:40:34.422
If we time it right,

00:40:34.498 --> 00:40:35.897
it should give us
enough momentum

00:40:35.966 --> 00:40:37.729
to outrun them
to the defense perimeter.

00:40:37.802 --> 00:40:40.293
We're going to use their
own weapons against them?

00:40:40.371 --> 00:40:41.702
The escape pods are away.

00:40:47.678 --> 00:40:50.010
Disengage the cloak.

00:40:52.216 --> 00:40:54.411
They've locked on.

00:40:55.453 --> 00:40:57.648
Sir?

00:40:57.721 --> 00:40:59.655
Not yet.

00:40:59.723 --> 00:41:02.487
Steady.

00:41:02.560 --> 00:41:03.822
Now!

00:41:09.133 --> 00:41:10.395
Status?

00:41:10.468 --> 00:41:11.730
Shields are failing.

00:41:11.802 --> 00:41:13.770
Four Annari vessels
are in pursuit.

00:41:13.838 --> 00:41:14.930
They're closing.

00:41:15.005 --> 00:41:16.336
Full thrusters!

00:41:18.342 --> 00:41:19.775
Shields are down.

00:41:19.844 --> 00:41:22.278
Get us through that defense
perimeter, Mr. Terek.

00:41:22.346 --> 00:41:24.439
Yes, sir.

00:41:31.522 --> 00:41:33.717
We're inside.

00:41:33.791 --> 00:41:35.986
The Annari have
broken off their pursuit.

00:41:38.796 --> 00:41:41.162
Take us to the surface,
Mr. Terek.

00:41:52.610 --> 00:41:55.078
We've just crossed out
of Annari space.

00:41:55.145 --> 00:41:56.339
Our escorts have broken off.

00:41:56.413 --> 00:41:57.402
They're going to warp.

00:41:57.481 --> 00:41:59.142
Bring the long-range sensors
on line.

00:41:59.216 --> 00:42:00.547
You and Tom, take the Flyer.

00:42:00.618 --> 00:42:03.052
Start your search
at Harry's last known position.

00:42:03.120 --> 00:42:04.781
Tuvok, send an
encrypted message

00:42:04.855 --> 00:42:06.186
to the Kraylor homeworld.

00:42:06.257 --> 00:42:08.418
See if they know where
Harry and Seven are.

00:42:08.492 --> 00:42:10.426
That won't be
necessary, Captain.

00:42:10.494 --> 00:42:12.189
Ensign Kim is hailing us.

00:42:12.263 --> 00:42:13.525
From where?

00:42:13.597 --> 00:42:14.859
A cloaked vessel.

00:42:14.932 --> 00:42:18.129
It's directly astern.

00:42:18.202 --> 00:42:22.662
Acting Captain's Personal Log,
Stardate 54282.5.

00:42:22.740 --> 00:42:23.798
Final entry.

00:42:23.874 --> 00:42:26.035
New cloaking systems
are being installed

00:42:26.110 --> 00:42:27.270
in other Kraylor ships,

00:42:27.344 --> 00:42:29.369
so I guess
the mission was a success.

00:42:29.446 --> 00:42:32.574
Still, I wish
I felt better about it.

00:42:34.518 --> 00:42:35.951
Welcome home.

00:42:36.020 --> 00:42:38.955
It's good to be back.

00:42:39.023 --> 00:42:41.924
So, what'll it be tonight?

00:42:41.992 --> 00:42:44.222
I have a light
Tula cheese soufflé

00:42:44.295 --> 00:42:46.195
or a zesty lasagna.

00:42:46.263 --> 00:42:49.255
You know, Neelix,
the truth is, I'm not sure.

00:42:49.333 --> 00:42:51.358
I thought
we talked about this.

00:42:51.435 --> 00:42:52.902
A Captain has to be deci...

00:42:52.970 --> 00:42:55.495
I'm not a Captain, Neelix.

00:42:58.542 --> 00:43:00.874
Not yet, anyway.
